IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc6-tests-support.l4 -- builders for the EXPECTED values of the tests, so that a test can state a punishment as the text writes it ("not more than 14 years ... a minimum ... of one year").
-- They are used only by the ccc6-tests-*.l4 and ccc6-cases-seat.l4 files; the encoding itself does not import them.

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN Imprisonment
`ss 150 to 182 test a term of years` MEANS `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF n, 0, 0, FALSE)

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN Imprisonment
`ss 150 to 182 test a term of months` MEANS `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, n, 0, FALSE)

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN Imprisonment
`ss 150 to 182 test a term of days` MEANS `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 0, 0, n, FALSE)

-- "two years less a day"
`ss 150 to 182 test a term of two years less a day` MEANS `imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 2, 0, 0, TRUE)

-- One indictable limb: the most and the least imprisonment, and no fine stated.
GIVEN most IS AN Imprisonment, least IS AN Imprisonment
GIVETH A Punishment
`ss 150 to 182 test an indictable punishment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, most, least, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- One summary limb.
GIVEN most IS AN Imprisonment, least IS AN Imprisonment
GIVETH A Punishment
`ss 150 to 182 test a summary punishment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, most, least, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- The class a section gives.
`ss 150 to 182 test both` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
